**Kill criteria:** if Pyramid does not beat the best single-agent baseline on cost per success by at least 30% on parallel-shaped tasks, or loses quality, do not ship it as the default. If an ablation shows a layer adds cost without quality, delete that layer.

## 17. Known unknowns

- No published evidence tests the merged planner-divider specifically; Phase 2 ablation should.
- Free-tier small models vary in tool-calling reliability; this is the most likely practical failure point.
- Self-created tool benchmarks come from project READMEs, so treat them as unverified.
- Router quality depends on logged data volume; expect the rules-first router to carry you for a while.
- Decentralized shared-context designs (one 2026 preprint reports large speedups) are promising but unreplicated; revisit after Phase 3.